"note": "Canonical and landing nothing. We ask flat `/rest/payslips` (deel.py:122); the endpoint is per Global-Payroll worker. THE PARENT EDGE IS UNPROVEN: Deel publishes no GP-worker listing (every `/rest/gp/workers/...` path is keyed by an id), and the only candidate enumeration is `GET /rest/contracts?types=[\"global_payroll\"]` → `data[].worker.id`. No Deel page states that id is the one this endpoint's `{id}` accepts, and `/rest/people` demonstrably carries two different worker identifiers, so the mapping needs a live call before it is built. EOR payslips are a separate, fully enumerable pair: `/rest/eor/workers/{worker_id}/payslips` with `/rest/people?hiring_types=[\"eor\"]`."
